-- 011_vera_topic_registry.sql
-- Filename deliberately does not match apply_migrations.py's `{prefix}_vera_*.sql` glob (same convention as 007/008-DRAFT); rename only at approval.
-- TOPICREG-1028 pre-stage DRAFT. NOT EXECUTED. Not a live migration: it sits in pending/ and is invisible to the runner.
-- NUMBER 011: 007 is the DAR domain registry (untouched; vera/dar_store.py uses it). 008 = schema_migrations bootstrap (reserved
-- by db/migration_guard.py), 009 = portal discovery, 010 = dynamic state, 011 = this topic registry, 012 = classifier categories.
-- Owner decision 2026-10-28: the topic registry is a separate new migration, not a revision of 007.
-- REQUIRES PostgreSQL 16 or newer: the role checks read pg_auth_members.inherit_option and .set_option (PG16+ columns).
-- Production was last observed as PG 18.6 on 2026-10-21; UNCONFIRMED since.
-- Replaces the in-config registry config/micro_topic_anchors.json (kept as SEED and FALLBACK). Owner: "when i speak of a table, i
-- mean in the database"; accepted Q6 (registry in the DB), Q7 (normalized unique keys; proposals need curator approval), Q8 (key
-- at acquisition), Q9 (read-time keying; backfill deferred).
-- APPLYING IT NEEDS OWNER-APPROVED DDL in that turn (AGENTS.md rule 4), admin-run only, never via db/apply_migrations.py --dry-run
-- (HZ-DAR-1). It is BATCHED with 008 and 010 under ONE PG 18 rehearsal on an isolated DB (none exists yet). The schema name
-- vera_vjay and roles vera_vjay_wo/_rw/_ro are copied from 006/007/008; the schema name is still UNCONFIRMED by the owner.
-- VERSIONING (OD-1028(40)-(43)): each version of a topic is its own row, UNIQUE (topic_key, version); at most one ACTIVE row per
--   key (partial unique index); activating a row retires the previously active row of that key in the same transaction (trigger);
--   content is IMMUTABLE after insert, only state may change (modified_at follows); no DELETE (retire instead).
-- APP-PROPOSED TOPICS: owner decisions 2026-10-28: the current list (the seed) is active; a topic the app creates is written as
--   'draft'; the app then checks it against the ACTIVE, RETIRED, BANNED, PROHIBITED and SECRETS topics and moves it draft -> 'suspended'
--   (similar to any of them) or draft -> 'active' (similar to neither); if the check cannot run it stays 'draft'. The DB enforces the
--   limits: an app role may INSERT only a BRAND-NEW key, version 1, origin 'runtime', state 'draft' (or a refused-topic state, see TOPICAL STATES); its ONLY UPDATEs are state
--   draft -> active and draft -> suspended on rows with origin 'runtime' (column-level GRANT UPDATE (state) to rw plus the guard
--   trigger, no SECURITY DEFINER). Every other change (other columns, other transitions, any seed row, DELETE, TRUNCATE) is
--   owner-only. The similarity check is app code (lexical, PROVISIONAL), not DB-enforced.
-- DUPLICATE vs DISTINCT (OD-1028(49), owner 2026-10-28): a 'match' means SEMANTIC EQUIVALENCE or PARAPHRASE only. A narrower
--   topic inside an active topic, or a broader non-equivalent topic, is a DISTINCT micro-topic and is activated. parent_topic_key
--   (nullable) records a known parent: supplied by the caller when the proposal context identifies one, never inferred by a
--   similarity threshold; it must reference an existing ACTIVE key at insert time and is immutable (content). No acquisition
--   cap or target is changed by this file.
-- PRIVILEGE (default deny): only the TABLE OWNER (current_user = the owner read from pg_catalog) is privileged; every other
--   role gets the app limits. The trigger itself has no role-membership test; the preflight below and the loader
--   (vera/topic_registry.py) check BOTH directions: the owner must not be an app role or hold a usable (INHERIT or SET)
--   membership in one, and no app role may be able to reach the owner. Run this file as the account that will own the table.
-- Trigger functions carry SET search_path = pg_catalog, pg_temp and schema-qualified references.
-- UNTESTED against a real PostgreSQL: triggers, partial unique indexes and CHECKs have never been executed.
-- Rollback (destructive, separate approval): db/migrations/rollback/011-DRAFT-topic-registry-rollback.sql.draft
-- REQUIRED ORDER: (1) roles via db/accounts/create_vera_accounts.sql, (2) migrations 001-005, (3) this file.
-- RUN WITH: psql -X -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -f <this file>   (no -1 needed: the file has its own BEGIN/COMMIT; ON_ERROR_STOP makes psql stop
-- at the first error, so the open transaction is never committed and PostgreSQL rolls everything back).
-- STRICTLY ADDITIVE: the first statement after BEGIN is the collision preflight; it RAISEs if the table or ANY function, trigger,
-- index or constraint this file creates already exists ("already applied or name collision"). All CREATEs are plain (no
-- existence-tolerant or replacing forms; CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS is the one exception); nothing existing is altered.
-- NAMING (OD-1028(50), owner 2026-10-28; work/additive-1028/NAMING.md): prefix topreg_ plus type suffixes _fn _trgfn _trg _idx _uq _chk _pk _fk.
-- TOPICAL STATES (OD-1028(51)/(52)): draft, active, suspended, retired, banned, prohibited, secrets. banned/prohibited/secrets rows
--   record REFUSED topic categories (category code in column field, neutral label; NEVER question text, OD-1028(35)). App roles may
--   INSERT a brand-new key only with state draft, banned, prohibited or secrets (DB-enforced); the app's only UPDATE stays
--   draft -> active or suspended; only the owner/admin may move a topic out of banned, prohibited or secrets.
-- LIVE-CALIBRATION LOG (TOPICJUDGE-1028, OD-1028(54), same feature, still unapplied): table topreg_judgments records each free-LLM
--   equivalence verdict (shadow or active mode) by KEYS and STATES only: NO question text, NO topic text (labels are reachable by key).
--   App rw may INSERT (column-level) and SELECT only: no UPDATE, DELETE or TRUNCATE grant; the daily judgment cap is counted from it.
BEGIN;

-- Collision preflight (strictly additive): stop cleanly if the table or ANY object this file creates already exists.
DO $$
DECLARE n text;
BEGIN
  IF pg_catalog.to_regclass('vera_vjay.topreg_topics') IS NOT NULL THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION '011 already applied or name collision';
  END IF;
  IF pg_catalog.to_regclass('vera_vjay.topreg_judgments') IS NOT NULL THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION '011 already applied or name collision';
  END IF;
  FOREACH n IN ARRAY ARRAY['topreg_is_owner_fn','topreg_guard_trgfn','topreg_forbid_truncate_trgfn','topreg_label_unique_trgfn','topreg_activate_trgfn'] LOOP
    IF EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM pg_catalog.pg_proc p JOIN pg_catalog.pg_namespace ns ON ns.oid = p.pronamespace
                WHERE p.proname = n AND ns.nspname = 'vera_vjay') THEN
      RAISE EXCEPTION '011 already applied or name collision';
    END IF;
  END LOOP;
  FOREACH n IN ARRAY ARRAY['topreg_topics_pk','topreg_key_version_uq','topreg_one_active_uq','topreg_active_label_uq','topreg_judgments_pk','topreg_judgments_draft_idx','topreg_judgments_created_idx'] LOOP
    IF EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM pg_catalog.pg_class c JOIN pg_catalog.pg_namespace ns ON ns.oid = c.relnamespace
                WHERE c.relname = n AND ns.nspname = 'vera_vjay') THEN
      RAISE EXCEPTION '011 already applied or name collision';
    END IF;
  END LOOP;
  FOREACH n IN ARRAY ARRAY['topreg_a_guard_trg','topreg_b_labels_trg','topreg_c_activate_trg','topreg_no_truncate_trg'] LOOP
    IF EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM pg_catalog.pg_trigger t JOIN pg_catalog.pg_class c ON c.oid = t.tgrelid
                JOIN pg_catalog.pg_namespace ns ON ns.oid = c.relnamespace
                WHERE t.tgname = n AND ns.nspname = 'vera_vjay') THEN
      RAISE EXCEPTION '011 already applied or name collision';
    END IF;
  END LOOP;
END $$;

DO $$ BEGIN
  IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM pg_catalog.pg_roles WHERE rolname = 'vera_vjay_wo')
     OR NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM pg_catalog.pg_roles WHERE rolname = 'vera_vjay_ro')
     OR NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM pg_catalog.pg_roles WHERE rolname = 'vera_vjay_rw') THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION '011 requires roles vera_vjay_wo, vera_vjay_rw and vera_vjay_ro (db/accounts/create_vera_accounts.sql first).';
  END IF;
END $$;

-- Preflight (R1, both directions): the table owner is unrestricted by the guard trigger, so this file must NOT run as an app role.
-- (1) Raises if current_user or session_user IS, or DIRECTLY holds a USABLE membership (inherit_option OR set_option, PG16+; an
-- ADMIN-only row, e.g. a CREATEROLE creator, does not count) in vera_vjay_wo / _rw / _ro.
-- (2) Raises if any app role is able to reach current_user or session_user (pg_has_role MEMBER, which follows inheritance), because
-- an app role that can become the owner would be unrestricted. Run it as the dedicated admin account that should own the table.
DO $$ BEGIN
  IF current_user IN ('vera_vjay_wo', 'vera_vjay_rw', 'vera_vjay_ro') OR session_user IN ('vera_vjay_wo', 'vera_vjay_rw', 'vera_vjay_ro')
     OR EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM pg_catalog.pg_auth_members m
                  JOIN pg_catalog.pg_roles r ON r.oid = m.roleid
                  JOIN pg_catalog.pg_roles u ON u.oid = m.member
                 WHERE r.rolname IN ('vera_vjay_wo', 'vera_vjay_rw', 'vera_vjay_ro')
                   AND (m.inherit_option OR m.set_option)
                   AND u.rolname IN (current_user::pg_catalog.text, session_user::pg_catalog.text)) THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION '011 must not run as, or as a member of, an app role (vera_vjay_wo/_rw/_ro): the table owner is unrestricted.';
  END IF;
  IF EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM pg_catalog.pg_roles a
              WHERE a.rolname IN ('vera_vjay_wo', 'vera_vjay_rw', 'vera_vjay_ro')
                AND (pg_catalog.pg_has_role(a.rolname, current_user, 'MEMBER') OR pg_catalog.pg_has_role(a.rolname, session_user, 'MEMBER'))) THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION '011: an app role (vera_vjay_wo/_rw/_ro) can reach the account running this file; it would reach the table owner.';
  END IF;
END $$;

CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS vera_vjay;

CREATE TABLE vera_vjay.topreg_topics (
    topic_row_id   BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY CONSTRAINT topreg_topics_pk PRIMARY KEY,
    -- topic_key: the NORMALIZED unique key (Q7): lowercase letters, digits, hyphen; app normalizes (NFKC, casefold, spaces to hyphen).
    topic_key      TEXT NOT NULL CONSTRAINT topreg_key_chk CHECK (topic_key ~ '^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{1,63}$'),
    -- version: NO DEFAULT. NULL on insert = next number (trigger); a supplied value must equal max+1.
    version        INTEGER NOT NULL CONSTRAINT topreg_version_chk CHECK (version >= 1),
    -- free text: printable ASCII only (no newline or control character), length-capped; never passed raw into prompts.
    label          TEXT NOT NULL CONSTRAINT topreg_label_chk
        CHECK (label ~ '^[ -~]+$' AND btrim(label) <> '' AND length(label) BETWEEN 3 AND 120),
    field          TEXT NOT NULL CONSTRAINT topreg_field_chk
        CHECK (field ~ '^[ -~]+$' AND btrim(field) <> '' AND length(field) BETWEEN 2 AND 60),
    anchor_text    TEXT NOT NULL CONSTRAINT topreg_anchor_chk
        CHECK (anchor_text ~ '^[ -~]+$' AND btrim(anchor_text) <> '' AND length(anchor_text) BETWEEN 20 AND 1200),
    parent_openalex_topic TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'none' CONSTRAINT topreg_parent_chk
        CHECK (parent_openalex_topic ~ '^[A-Za-z0-9:_./-]{1,64}$'),
    -- parent_topic_key (OD-1028(49)): nullable, content (immutable). Well-formed key; the guard trigger requires it to reference an
    -- existing ACTIVE key at insert time. Supplied by the caller only; never inferred by a similarity threshold.
    parent_topic_key TEXT CONSTRAINT topreg_parent_key_chk CHECK (parent_topic_key IS NULL OR parent_topic_key ~ '^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{1,63}$'),
    origin         TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'runtime' CONSTRAINT topreg_origin_chk CHECK (origin IN ('seed','runtime')),
    state          TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'draft' CONSTRAINT topreg_state_chk
        CHECK (state IN ('draft','active','suspended','retired','banned','prohibited','secrets')),
    created_at     TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    modified_at    TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    CONSTRAINT topreg_key_version_uq UNIQUE (topic_key, version)
);

-- At most one active row per key; at most one active row per normalized label.
CREATE UNIQUE INDEX topreg_one_active_uq ON vera_vjay.topreg_topics (topic_key) WHERE state = 'active';
CREATE UNIQUE INDEX topreg_active_label_uq
    ON vera_vjay.topreg_topics ((pg_catalog.lower(pg_catalog.regexp_replace(pg_catalog.btrim(label), '\s+', ' ', 'g')))) WHERE state = 'active';

-- Privileged = the table owner only (default deny). Everyone else, including other admins, gets the app limits.
CREATE FUNCTION vera_vjay.topreg_is_owner_fn() RETURNS boolean LANGUAGE sql STABLE
  SET search_path = pg_catalog, pg_temp AS $f$
  SELECT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM pg_catalog.pg_class c
                  WHERE c.oid = 'vera_vjay.topreg_topics'::pg_catalog.regclass
                    AND pg_catalog.pg_get_userbyid(c.relowner) = current_user)
$f$;

-- Fires first (trigger name order): non-owner limits, version numbering, content immutability.
CREATE FUNCTION vera_vjay.topreg_guard_trgfn() RETURNS trigger LANGUAGE plpgsql
  SET search_path = pg_catalog, pg_temp AS $f$
DECLARE
  is_owner boolean := vera_vjay.topreg_is_owner_fn();
  nxt integer;
BEGIN
  IF NOT is_owner AND TG_OP = 'DELETE' THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'topreg_topics: DELETE not allowed for app roles';
  END IF;
  IF NOT is_owner AND TG_OP = 'UPDATE' AND (OLD.origin <> 'runtime' OR OLD.state <> 'draft' OR NEW.state NOT IN ('active','suspended')) THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'topreg_topics: app roles may only move a runtime draft row to active or suspended (leaving banned/prohibited/secrets is owner-only)';
  END IF;
  IF TG_OP = 'DELETE' THEN
    RETURN OLD;                                   -- owner only; retire instead (returning NULL would cancel the DELETE)
  END IF;
  IF TG_OP = 'INSERT' THEN
    SELECT COALESCE(max(t.version), 0) + 1 INTO nxt FROM vera_vjay.topreg_topics t WHERE t.topic_key = NEW.topic_key;
    IF NOT is_owner THEN
      IF nxt <> 1 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION 'topreg_topics: app roles may insert only brand-new keys';
      END IF;
      IF NEW.origin <> 'runtime' OR NEW.state NOT IN ('draft','banned','prohibited','secrets') OR NEW.parent_openalex_topic <> 'none' THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION 'topreg_topics: app roles may insert only origin=runtime, state=draft/banned/prohibited/secrets, no OpenAlex parent topic';
      END IF;
      IF NEW.state <> 'draft' AND NEW.parent_topic_key IS NOT NULL THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION 'topreg_topics: a refused-topic row (banned/prohibited/secrets) has no parent topic key';
      END IF;
      NEW.created_at := now();                    -- accounting fields are not caller-controlled
    END IF;
    IF NEW.parent_topic_key IS NOT NULL THEN
      IF NEW.parent_topic_key = NEW.topic_key THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION 'topreg_topics: a topic cannot be its own parent';
      END IF;
      IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM vera_vjay.topreg_topics p WHERE p.topic_key = NEW.parent_topic_key AND p.state = 'active') THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION 'topreg_topics: parent_topic_key must reference an existing active topic key';
      END IF;
    END IF;
    IF NEW.version IS NULL THEN
      NEW.version := nxt;
    ELSIF NEW.version <> nxt THEN
      RAISE EXCEPTION 'topreg_topics: version % is wrong for key %, expected %', NEW.version, NEW.topic_key, nxt;
    END IF;
    NEW.modified_at := NEW.created_at;
    RETURN NEW;
  END IF;
  -- UPDATE (owner, or an app role's draft -> active above): content is immutable for everyone; only state may change.
  IF NEW.topic_key IS DISTINCT FROM OLD.topic_key OR NEW.version IS DISTINCT FROM OLD.version
     OR NEW.label IS DISTINCT FROM OLD.label OR NEW.field IS DISTINCT FROM OLD.field
     OR NEW.anchor_text IS DISTINCT FROM OLD.anchor_text OR NEW.parent_openalex_topic IS DISTINCT FROM OLD.parent_openalex_topic
     OR NEW.parent_topic_key IS DISTINCT FROM OLD.parent_topic_key
     OR NEW.origin IS DISTINCT FROM OLD.origin OR NEW.created_at IS DISTINCT FROM OLD.created_at
     OR NEW.topic_row_id IS DISTINCT FROM OLD.topic_row_id THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'topreg_topics: content is immutable; insert a new version instead (only state may change)';
  END IF;
  IF NEW.state IS DISTINCT FROM OLD.state THEN
    NEW.modified_at := now();
  ELSE
    NEW.modified_at := OLD.modified_at;
  END IF;
  RETURN NEW;
END $f$;

CREATE FUNCTION vera_vjay.topreg_forbid_truncate_trgfn() RETURNS trigger LANGUAGE plpgsql
  SET search_path = pg_catalog, pg_temp AS $f$
BEGIN
  IF NOT vera_vjay.topreg_is_owner_fn() THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'topreg_topics: TRUNCATE not allowed for app roles';
  END IF;
  RETURN NULL;
END $f$;

-- A normalized label may belong to only ONE key (any state): a duplicate topic under another key is rejected (Q7).
CREATE FUNCTION vera_vjay.topreg_label_unique_trgfn() RETURNS trigger LANGUAGE plpgsql
  SET search_path = pg_catalog, pg_temp AS $f$
BEGIN
  IF EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM vera_vjay.topreg_topics t
              WHERE t.topic_key <> NEW.topic_key
                AND pg_catalog.lower(pg_catalog.regexp_replace(pg_catalog.btrim(t.label), '\s+', ' ', 'g'))
                  = pg_catalog.lower(pg_catalog.regexp_replace(pg_catalog.btrim(NEW.label), '\s+', ' ', 'g'))) THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'topreg_topics: label already belongs to another topic key';
  END IF;
  RETURN NEW;
END $f$;

-- Activation: when a row becomes active, the OTHER active row of the same key (if one exists) becomes retired, same transaction.
-- BEFORE trigger so the old row is retired before the partial unique index sees the new active row. The UPDATE runs only if
-- another active row exists (so an app-role insert of a brand-new active key performs no UPDATE).
CREATE FUNCTION vera_vjay.topreg_activate_trgfn() RETURNS trigger LANGUAGE plpgsql
  SET search_path = pg_catalog, pg_temp AS $f$
BEGIN
  IF NEW.state = 'active' AND (TG_OP = 'INSERT' OR OLD.state IS DISTINCT FROM 'active') THEN
    IF EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM vera_vjay.topreg_topics c
                WHERE c.topic_key = NEW.topic_key AND c.state = 'active' AND c.topic_row_id IS DISTINCT FROM NEW.topic_row_id) THEN
      UPDATE vera_vjay.topreg_topics c SET state = 'retired', modified_at = now()
       WHERE c.topic_key = NEW.topic_key AND c.state = 'active' AND c.topic_row_id IS DISTINCT FROM NEW.topic_row_id;
    END IF;
  END IF;
  RETURN NEW;
END $f$;

CREATE TRIGGER topreg_a_guard_trg BEFORE INSERT OR UPDATE OR DELETE ON vera_vjay.topreg_topics
  FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION vera_vjay.topreg_guard_trgfn();
CREATE TRIGGER topreg_b_labels_trg BEFORE INSERT ON vera_vjay.topreg_topics
  FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION vera_vjay.topreg_label_unique_trgfn();
CREATE TRIGGER topreg_c_activate_trg BEFORE INSERT OR UPDATE ON vera_vjay.topreg_topics
  FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION vera_vjay.topreg_activate_trgfn();
CREATE TRIGGER topreg_no_truncate_trg BEFORE TRUNCATE ON vera_vjay.topreg_topics
  FOR EACH STATEMENT EXECUTE FUNCTION vera_vjay.topreg_forbid_truncate_trgfn();

-- TOPICJUDGE-1028 live-calibration log: keys, states and the verdict only (no question text, no topic text). Append-only for the app.
CREATE TABLE vera_vjay.topreg_judgments (
    id              BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY CONSTRAINT topreg_judgments_pk PRIMARY KEY,
    draft_key       TEXT NOT NULL CONSTRAINT topreg_jdraft_key_chk CHECK (draft_key ~ '^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{1,63}$'),
    candidate_key   TEXT NOT NULL CONSTRAINT topreg_jcand_key_chk CHECK (candidate_key ~ '^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{1,63}$'),
    candidate_state TEXT NOT NULL CONSTRAINT topreg_jcand_state_chk CHECK (candidate_state IN ('active','retired','banned','prohibited','secrets')),
    verdict         TEXT NOT NULL CONSTRAINT topreg_jverdict_chk CHECK (verdict IN ('yes','no','unknown')),
    mode            TEXT NOT NULL CONSTRAINT topreg_jmode_chk CHECK (mode IN ('shadow','active')),
    model_id        TEXT NOT NULL CONSTRAINT topreg_jmodel_chk CHECK (model_id ~ '^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._:/-]{0,79}$'),
    latency_ms      INTEGER NOT NULL CONSTRAINT topreg_jlatency_chk CHECK (latency_ms >= 0),
    created_at      TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now()
);
CREATE INDEX topreg_judgments_draft_idx ON vera_vjay.topreg_judgments (draft_key);
CREATE INDEX topreg_judgments_created_idx ON vera_vjay.topreg_judgments (created_at);

-- Seed: the 10 entries of config/micro_topic_anchors.json (owner-run, origin 'seed', version 1, active). Idempotent: a key
-- that already has any row is skipped (no ON CONFLICT: the version is trigger-assigned only when NULL).
INSERT INTO vera_vjay.topreg_topics (topic_key, version, label, field, anchor_text, parent_openalex_topic, origin, state)
SELECT v.topic_key, v.version, v.label, v.field, v.anchor_text, v.parent_openalex_topic, v.origin, v.state
  FROM (VALUES
    ('epi-infectious-outbreak', 1, 'Infectious disease outbreak epidemiology', 'epidemiology', 'epidemiology infectious disease outbreak transmission incidence prevalence surveillance cohort case-control mortality morbidity reproduction number vaccination vaccine efficacy seroprevalence pandemic epidemic contact tracing risk factors population health public health intervention confidence interval odds ratio hazard ratio cases deaths hospitalization pathogen infection viral bacterial symptoms outbreak investigation modelling serological estimates', 'none', 'seed', 'active'),
    ('epi-chronic-cohort', 1, 'Chronic disease cohort and risk epidemiology', 'epidemiology', 'cohort study chronic disease cardiovascular cancer diabetes obesity risk factors incidence relative risk longitudinal follow-up participants exposure smoking diet physical activity mortality hazard ratio adjusted confounding observational study population-based registry screening prevention randomized trial meta-analysis systematic review epidemiological association prospective cohort bias sample size questionnaire incidence rates health outcomes', 'none', 'seed', 'active'),
    ('eco-biodiversity', 1, 'Biodiversity and species ecology', 'ecology', 'ecology biodiversity species richness abundance habitat conservation extinction population dynamics community ecosystem functional diversity trophic food web invasive species predator prey biomass forest wetland grassland survey conservation biology endangered ecological niche field sampling transect census taxa diversity index species distribution wildlife monitoring protected areas', 'none', 'seed', 'active'),
    ('eco-ecosystem-function', 1, 'Ecosystem function and nutrient cycling', 'ecology', 'ecosystem productivity nutrient cycling nitrogen phosphorus carbon soil microbial decomposition primary production photosynthesis plant growth freshwater marine lake river watershed disturbance fire resilience succession land use restoration vegetation ecosystem services carbon storage greenhouse flux plant litter microbial community biogeochemical ecological processes field experiment', 'none', 'seed', 'active'),
    ('clim-warming', 1, 'Climate change and global warming', 'climate science', 'climate change global warming temperature anomaly greenhouse gas emissions carbon dioxide radiative forcing climate sensitivity sea level rise ice sheet glacier ocean heat uptake IPCC scenario projection attribution extreme weather heatwave drought precipitation atmospheric warming mitigation adaptation climate observations global mean surface temperature trend carbon budget emissions pathways warming impacts', 'none', 'seed', 'active'),
    ('clim-modelling', 1, 'Climate modelling and projections', 'climate science', 'climate model simulation general circulation model CMIP ensemble downscaling bias correction reanalysis atmosphere ocean coupled model parameterization uncertainty internal variability ENSO monsoon aerosol cloud feedback paleoclimate reconstruction observational record forecast skill regional climate model resolution validation observations uncertainty quantification climate projections scenarios', 'none', 'seed', 'active'),
    ('repro-research', 1, 'Research reproducibility and open science', 'reproducibility and software practice', 'reproducibility replication crisis open science preregistration data sharing transparency statistical power p-hacking publication bias replicability research integrity FAIR principles metadata provenance reproducible workflow computational reproducibility version control containers peer review registered report research practices questionable results scientific rigor open data code availability reporting standards guidelines', 'none', 'seed', 'active'),
    ('repro-software', 1, 'Research software engineering practice', 'reproducibility and software practice', 'research software engineering scientific software testing continuous integration code review documentation version control git open source package dependency management software sustainability technical debt best practices unit tests reproducible build notebooks scripts developers maintainability software citation software quality research code practices survey scientists programming skills training testing workflows', 'none', 'seed', 'active'),
    ('aicode-assistants', 1, 'AI coding assistants and code generation', 'AI coding assistants', 'AI coding assistant large language model code generation Copilot ChatGPT programming developers productivity code completion program synthesis prompt benchmark HumanEval pass rate bugs vulnerabilities security code quality software engineering autocomplete pair programming empirical study students novices software developers experiment tool usage accuracy generated programs educational computing study', 'none', 'seed', 'active'),
    ('aicode-agents-eval', 1, 'LLM coding agents and evaluation', 'AI coding assistants', 'LLM agent software engineering automated program repair issue resolution SWE-bench test generation code review hallucination evaluation trust developer experience controlled experiment agentic tool use repository-level code language models fine-tuning debugging refactoring maintainability adoption survey software maintenance benchmark tasks agents autonomy limitations evaluation metrics generated patches', 'none', 'seed', 'active')
  ) AS v(topic_key, version, label, field, anchor_text, parent_openalex_topic, origin, state)
 WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM vera_vjay.topreg_topics t WHERE t.topic_key = v.topic_key);

-- Default deny, then exact grants. REVOKE ALL first so no inherited or earlier grant survives. rw gets column-level INSERT on only
-- the columns the app supplies: topic_row_id (identity), version, created_at, modified_at and parent_openalex_topic are NOT
-- grantable to it, so rw cannot choose topic_row_id (no OVERRIDING SYSTEM VALUE) and thereby the loader's ORDER BY.
REVOKE ALL ON vera_vjay.topreg_topics FROM PUBLIC, vera_vjay_wo, vera_vjay_rw, vera_vjay_ro;
GRANT SELECT ON vera_vjay.topreg_topics TO vera_vjay_ro;
GRANT SELECT ON vera_vjay.topreg_topics TO vera_vjay_rw;
GRANT INSERT (topic_key, label, field, anchor_text, parent_topic_key, origin, state) ON vera_vjay.topreg_topics TO vera_vjay_rw;
GRANT UPDATE (state) ON vera_vjay.topreg_topics TO vera_vjay_rw;   -- draft -> active/suspended of runtime rows only (guard trigger)
-- topreg_judgments: app rw may SELECT and INSERT only (no UPDATE, DELETE, TRUNCATE); id and created_at are not grantable to it.
REVOKE ALL ON vera_vjay.topreg_judgments FROM PUBLIC, vera_vjay_wo, vera_vjay_rw, vera_vjay_ro;
GRANT SELECT ON vera_vjay.topreg_judgments TO vera_vjay_ro;
GRANT SELECT ON vera_vjay.topreg_judgments TO vera_vjay_rw;
GRANT INSERT (draft_key, candidate_key, candidate_state, verdict, mode, model_id, latency_ms) ON vera_vjay.topreg_judgments TO vera_vjay_rw;

COMMIT;
